('A telescope photometer measures brightness across consecutive observations. A periodic dip in a star light curve can indicate a transiting planet.','What signal in stellar brightness suggests a planetary transit?','What quantity is recorded in a photometric time series?'),
('A differential privacy mechanism adds calibrated random noise to limit how much one individual changes an output distribution. The privacy parameter epsilon controls the permitted privacy loss.','What role does epsilon play in differential privacy?','Why is randomized noise added to a private statistical release?'),
('The robot estimates its pose from inertial measurements and camera features. Sensor fusion combines complementary information to reduce uncertainty compared with either source alone.','Why combine visual features with inertial readings for robot localization?','What state does the robot estimate from camera and IMU data?'),
('An event-driven service publishes immutable events to a broker. Consumers track offsets so they can resume processing after a restart.','How can a message consumer continue after restarting?','What data is published in the event-driven service?'),
